@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Terms of Service";
}

<section class="py-5">
    <div class="container" style="max-width:800px;">

        <div class="text-center mb-5">
            <img src="/images/Logo.png" alt="BoredGamers Logo" style="max-width:280px;width:100%;">
        </div>

        <h2 class="text-center mb-2">Terms of Service</h2>
        <p class="text-center text-muted mb-5"><small>Last updated: May 2026 (probably)</small></p>

        <div class="card bg-dark mb-4">
            <div class="card-body">
                <h5 class="card-title">1. Welcome, Fellow Bored Gamer</h5>
                <p class="card-text text-muted">
                    By accessing BoredGamers, you agree to these Terms of Service. If you do not agree, please close this tab,
                    go outside, touch some grass, and reconsider your life choices. Then come back, because we'd really love
                    to have you here.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="card bg-dark mb-4">
            <div class="card-body">
                <h5 class="card-title">2. Acceptable Use</h5>
                <p class="card-text text-muted">
                    You agree to use BoredGamers for the purpose of talking about board games, not for anything nefarious,
                    illegal, or deeply uncool. This includes but is not limited to: spamming, harassing other users,
                    pretending Monopoly is a good game, or arguing that Risk can be finished in under four hours.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="card bg-dark mb-4">
            <div class="card-body">
                <h5 class="card-title">3. User Content</h5>
                <p class="card-text text-muted">
                    Anything you post (reviews, comments, hot takes about Catan) remains yours. You just grant us a
                    non-exclusive, royalty-free license to display it on the platform. We promise not to sell your
                    controversial opinion that Ticket to Ride is overrated to any advertising agencies. Probably.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="card bg-dark mb-4">
            <div class="card-body">
                <h5 class="card-title">4. Account Responsibility</h5>
                <p class="card-text text-muted">
                    You are responsible for keeping your account secure. If someone else gets into your account and
                    rates Candyland five stars, that's on you. Choose a strong password. Not "password123." Not your
                    dog's name. Something good. You know what to do.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="card bg-dark mb-4">
            <div class="card-body">
                <h5 class="card-title">5. Prohibited Conduct</h5>
                <p class="card-text text-muted">
                    The following activities are strictly forbidden: bullying other users, posting spam, attempting to hack
                    the platform, and — most critically — revealing the ending of any mystery board game in a public post
                    without a spoiler warning. We are very serious about that last one.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="card bg-dark mb-4">
            <div class="card-body">
                <h5 class="card-title">6. Limitation of Liability</h5>
                <p class="card-text text-muted">
                    BoredGamers is not responsible for any friendships lost, family dinners ruined, or sleep deprived due to
                    "just one more game." We warned you. The dice did not. BoredGamers is provided as-is, and while we try
                    our best, we make no guarantees that the site will be bug-free, always available, or capable of stopping
                    you from buying another board game you don't have shelf space for.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="card bg-dark mb-4">
            <div class="card-body">
                <h5 class="card-title">7. Changes to These Terms</h5>
                <p class="card-text text-muted">
                    We reserve the right to update these Terms at any time. We'll try to let you know when we do, but
                    we're a small team and things get hectic. By continuing to use BoredGamers after any changes, you agree
                    to the new Terms. By continuing to play Gloomhaven, you agree to never have free weekends again.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="card bg-dark mb-4">
            <div class="card-body">
                <h5 class="card-title">8. Governing Law</h5>
                <p class="card-text text-muted">
                    These Terms are governed by the laws of the great state of Oregon, and also by the house rules
                    your friend group has been using since 2019 that nobody wrote down but everyone vaguely agrees on.
                    In the event of any dispute, we suggest settling it with a friendly game of your choice.
                    Whoever wins is right.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="card bg-dark mb-4">
            <div class="card-body">
                <h5 class="card-title">9. Contact Us</h5>
                <p class="card-text text-muted">
                    Have questions about these Terms? Concerns? Suggestions? Just want to talk about board games?
                    Head over to our <a asp-controller="Home" asp-action="Contact" class="text-light">Contact page</a>
                    and reach out to the team. We actually read our emails. Most of the time.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <p class="text-center text-muted mt-5">
            <small>Thank you for reading the Terms of Service. You are one of approximately seven people who have ever done this. We respect that.</small>
        </p>

    </div>
</section>
